    {
      "id": 586,
      "url": "/battlemap?incident=586",
      "dtg": "1967-08-06T11:00:00",
      "why": [
        "significant"
      ],
      "role": "Fire support",
      "ledBy": "7 RAR",
      "operation": "Ballarat",
      "task": "Bunker",
      "gridRef": "YS344742",
      "friendlyForce": 90,
      "enemyForce": 110,
      "friendlyKilled": 6,
      "friendlyWounded": 19,
      "enemyKilled": 15,
      "enemyWounded": 25,
      "units": [
        "106 Field Battery, 4 Field Regiment",
        "2 Battalion, 35 Field Artillery Regiment, US Army",
        "A Company, 7 Battalion, Royal Australian Regiment"
      ],
      "subUnits": [
        "106-field-battery"
      ],
      "report": "7 RAR was part of a search and destroy operation in the Hat Dich area. Camps and bunker systems were to be located and ambushed prior to being destroyed by shellfire and attack. A Coy had been inserted by stealth to ambush camp trails. At 1040hrs it had found a well used track and 2 pl had set a simple ambush. Within minutes 2 enemy with rifles slung wandered into the ambush and were shot dead with a burst of M60 fire. (see record 1050hrs).\n\nThe Coy CO estimated that an enemy squad was back along the track and sent 2 pl to make contact and brought in arty to cutoff the retreat of the enemy. 100yds along the track 2 pl ran into heavy automatic fire from an enemy defensive position. 1 pl was sent to make a right flanking attack but was stopped by an enemy pl. 7 enemy MGs were firing at 30m range at 6 Aust MGs. The rest of A coy was committed with support from airstrikes and arty. The enemy replied with rockets, grenades, MGs and SAs. At 1430hrs the enemy withdrew under intense arty and airstrike pressure. Enemy were protecting the withdrawal of enemy Bn from Bn camp 1km away. En had been 2nd Coy of 3 Bn of 274 Regt plus recon pl.\n\n 6 Aust were killed and 20 wounded; 12 Aust were only wounded slightly. The enemy. An estimated 15 enemy were killed and 25 wounded. Losses inflicted by arty and airstrike were estimated to be a further 200 (Noted in Arty Air Themes).\n\n106 Fd Bty and A Bty 2/35 engaged six locations in support of A Coy causing considerable enemy cas. (AWM95 3/7/2.pdf p48 4 Fd Regt Diary) \n\nYS344742: THE LEADING ELEMENTS OF A 7 RAR CONTACTED ANESTIMATED PL OF VC AT LOC STATED. A-S AND ARTY SUPPORTEDAND THE VC BROKE CONTACT AT 1230H, WITHDRAWING NTH AND NE.RES FRIENDLY CAS 6 AUST KIA AND 17 AUST WIA (CORRECTEDFIGURE FROM TELEGRAPHIC INTSUM) AND VC CAS 5 KIA (BC).DOCS TAKEN FROM THE BODIES IDENTIFIED THE UNIT AS C12 (2NDCOY) OF 3 BN 274 REGT. THE FOLLOWING WPNS, AMMO AND EQUIPMENTWERE CAPTURED;- 3 X AK47 RIFLES, 1 X CHICOM RPD LMG, 1 X B40AND 3 ROCKETS, 2 X M1 BAYONETS, 3 X BELTS WITH WATER BOTTLES,1 SMALL 1ST AID KIT, 1 X STICK GRENADE (HOMEMADE), 1 X WALLETAND DOCS, 2 PAIRS OF HO CHI MINH SANDALS, 1 SMALL BUNDLE OFCLOTHING, 300 RDS OF 7.62MM AK47 AMMO, 168 RDS ON A BELT(FOR LMG), 16 X AK47 MAGS.",
      "archivalSource": "Intsum, AWM95 1/4/55.pdf p172; AWM279 569/R4/66; On the Offensive pg210-216; Horner Arty pg 483;"
    },
    {
      "id": 697,
