      "subUnits": [
        "108-field-battery"
      ],
      "report": "Several enemy penetrated the defence perimeter of 108 Fd Bty and laid 4 claymore mines. Two were subsequently fired wounding and killing one gunner. 2 mines did not go off. Most of 108 Fd Bty were on duty otherwise the casualties would have been higher because the mines were aimed at the sleeping quarters.",
      "archivalSource": "On the Offensive pg261; AWM95 7-7-20.pdf 7 RAR Jan 68 pg8; Intsum, 1/4/69.pdf p143;"
    },
