      "task": "Bunker",
      "gridRef": "YS402780",
      "friendlyForce": 29,
      "enemyForce": 13,
      "friendlyKilled": 1,
      "friendlyWounded": 3,
      "enemyKilled": 1,
      "enemyWounded": 0,
      "units": [
        "1 APC Squadron, 3 Cavalry Regiment",
        "1 Armoured Regiment",
        "107 Field Battery, 4 Field Regiment",
        "8 Platoon, C Company, 8 Battalion, Royal Australian Regiment",
        "Light Fire Team"
      ],
      "subUnits": [],
      "report": "YS402780 8/B/8RAR FIRED ON FROM BKR SYSTEM. EN STR AT LEAST5. EN INITIALLY WDR SW FOR A SHORT DISTANCE AND THEN RE-ENGAGEDFRI FORCES. RES: 1 VC KIA (BC), QTY DOCUS CIA, 1 AUST KIA, 3AUST WIA. \n\nSee Combined Arms Data Base\n\nPl was following new track when it saw 2 enemy near a bunker. It opened fire killing one enemy. Heavy fire was opened from two bunkers pinning the forward section and 2 Aust cas were suffered at this stage. The enemy began to withdraw and the 2 Aust casualties were withdrawn to dustoff point. The enemy then reoccupied the bunkers opening fire and causing 2 more casualties. These were evacuated under cover of fire by an LFT and a resupply of ammo took place by helo. Aust cas were caused by 1x gren, 1xRPG, 2xAK47. After holding the enemy for an hour the pl withdrew 800m to allow arty bombardment and to marry up with tank troop and APC troop. The assault launched later that day met no resistance.\n\n161 Fd Bty, C/2/35 US Arty and A/7/8 US Arty fired in support (AWM95 3/7/13.pdf p14 4 Fd Regt Diary)",
      "archivalSource": "Intsum, AWM95 1/4/192.pdf p133; AWM 290 8/15 Cung Chung 1; AWM95 7-8-10.pdf 8 RAR Jun 70 pg77 Contact Rept;"
    },
    {
